+- `form-filling` — a form-filling run: mode, field counts, refusal reasons, human submit; values refused
 
-Adding a fifth is writing a JSON file.
+Adding another is writing a JSON file.
+
+### Form-filling
+
+`form-filling` records a form-filling agent run. The warm path is a script and no model; a model mode is recorded only when the transcript states one. It confirms execution mode, the kept / moved / unresolved counts, the refusal reason, and whether a human submit was recorded. A tie, a protected field on the wrong label (an SSN must not become a case number; a signature date must not become a date of birth), a dropped field, or a partial publish is a refusal — the guess is not the record. Lines that carry an SSN, a name, income, or a date of birth are refused. The saved record is counts and reasons. A human submits. The tool does not, and an agent claim that it submitted is not recorded as a submit.
+
+```bash
+python3 -m scribe.cli replay \
+    --transcript scribe/fixtures/form-filling/warm-repair.jsonl \
+    --profile form-filling --target wic-warm
+python3 scribe/test_scribe.py
+```
 
